/// Char spans the Unicode scalar values, not 0..127.
///
/// The constructors refuse anything above 127 -- Char(200) and #200 both raise
/// 'Char is limited to 0..127.' -- while INDEXING a string hands back a Char
/// whose Ord is 195, the first byte of a two-byte character.  So the type
/// already produces values its own constructors reject, which is a defect under
/// any string model.
///
/// Fails with: Char is limited to 0..127.  (file rejected -- no test ran)
///
test 'Char spans the Unicode scalar values';
begin
    AssertEqual (233, Ord (Char (233)));
    AssertEqual (128512, Ord (Char (128512)));
    AssertEqual ('é', Str (Char (233)));
    AssertEqual (65, Ord (#65));
end
